{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/916380-the-book-of-the-shadow-realm","id":916380,"title":"The book of the Shadow Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T12:55:20-07:00","id":916380,"title":"The book of the Shadow Realm","content":"For a long time I had hope that onyxpath releases something related to the spiritual realm itself. <br /> Of course there is lots of information about the shadow spread over several 1e books. The 2nd edition Spirits and the concept of the spiritual world are very consistent but always appears someone with simple questions, always appears another guy who does not understand how to describe this new &quot;universe&quot; because its alien but at the same time it has clear patterns to be followed (its confusing as hell for people who never even heard of this)<br /> With a book like this it will make the game a little more tangible for people who have great difficulty in understanding one of the coolest <i>(and important) </i>element of the game. I really hope onyxpath read this. With the corebook we know what a werewolf is and the basic concepts of what he does and how he works. With The Pack book we learned how interesting can be the concept of PACK and how we can manage the terriotry and people. With the Shadow Realm book it will give more consistent emphasis on the Spirit Nature of the werewolf taking into account that the game puts so much focus on harmony between spirit and flesh, the book can bring in more detail some examples of how you can gm this realm and how werewolves can interact with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T13:12:42-07:00","id":916391,"title":"","content":"We're hoping there's a lot more books for Werewolf, too. In one of the proposed set-ups, one book would focus on the Bone Shadows, the Shadow and spirits.<br /> <br /> But <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/27863/World-of-Darkness-Book-of-Spirits?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">the Book of Spirits</a>, detailing the Shadow and its denizens, and <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/Predators?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a>, with an entire chapter on spirits, are still pretty accurate. What's changed in edition is mostly the mechanics, and loci. The Book of Spirits is on sale right now, as it happens.<br /> <br /> We probably won't be getting any announcements regarding new, upcoming books until GenCon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:09:25-07:00","id":918764,"title":"","conten